{"content":[{"c":["ABDON (P",{"c":["lace"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of four cities in Asher’s territory given to the Levites after the conquest of Canaan, the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.21.30","r":"Josh.21.30","rawR":"Josh.21.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.21.30","value":"Josh.21.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 21:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.74","r":"1Chr.6.74","rawR":"1Chr.6.74","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.74","value":"1Chr.6.74"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:74"},"). Abdon is probably the same as Ebron (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.28","r":"Josh.19.28","rawR":"Josh.19.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.28","value":"Josh.19.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:28"},"). Today Abdon is called Khirbet ’Abdeh."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AbdonPlace","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 21:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.21.30","rawQueryValue":"Josh.21.30","sourceRefExact":"Josh.21.30"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:74","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.74","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.74","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.74"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.28","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.28","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b2840520f7de367f6f40fad2d3400f6fadeca02b9311708ff67d5a95a4d0f89b","sourceItemName":"AbdonPlace","sourceItemOrder":15,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AbdonPlace","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Abdon (Place)","title":"Abdon (Place)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}